    <l n="1" para="true">ephippiis solo deturbentur ca-</l>
    <l n="2">taphractati,lapsuque graviore,</l>
    <l n="3">quo pondere magis obruütur,</l>
    <l n="4">si non intereant, saltem pericu-</l>
    <l n="5">lose lædantur. Unde etiam in-</l>
    <l n="6">ter Græcos sapientiores, qui</l>
    <l n="7">vel pueris talia exercitia per-</l>
    <l n="8">miserunt, eos, ut absque peri-</l>
    <l n="9">culo artis equestris, aliorum</l>
    <l n="10">exercitiorum rudimenta addi-</l>
    <l n="11">scerent, dorsis arietum, ne ex</l>
    <l n="12">alto laberentur, imponebant.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Metus insuper est, ne lan-</l>
    <l n="14">ceis in adversum directis ictu</l>
    <l n="15">quo vulnerentur, aut iisdem</l>
    <l n="16">fractis, alibi particula cassidem</l>
    <l n="17">subintret. Quomodo maximo</l>
    <l n="18">cum discrimine Cesennæ ex-</l>
    <l n="19">hiberi solitas fuisse illas decur-</l>
    <l n="20">siones, propter crassiores ha-</l>
    <l n="21">stas &amp; præpilatas, quibus no-</l>
    <l n="22">biles inter se concurrebant te-</l>
    <l n="23">stis est Gabriel Naudeus.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">2. Quia hoc genus haftilu-</l>
    <l n="25">dii nullam hodie utilitatem</l>
    <l n="26">adferre poterit. Majore quippe</l>
